Q: Re-render component onClick in reactjs A: <p>By looking at your your code I think You don't need forceUpdate here . what you need is a callback function,inside  that you need to  call setState. This will re render your component.</p>

<pre><code>    this.props.submitvote(vote_object,this.successfunction);
</code></pre>

<p>your Submitvote()  method should be like </p>

<pre><code>    submitvote(vote_object, success) { 

  success()
}
</code></pre>

